{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"121379","commit":"e68053e6a80b458bdd8fa713b129b844ef05b5b4","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The `waitForRateLimitingAssignments` helper only asserts that the `elastic` service with `TaskType.SPARSE_EMBEDDING` has a non-empty assignment. However, several of the tests that call it (e.g., `testNumberOfNodesPerGroup_Decreases_When_NodeLeavesCluster`, `testGrouping_RespectsMaxNodesPerGroupingLimit`, `testInitialRateLimitsCalculation_Correct`, `testRateLimits_Decrease_OnNodeJoin`, `testRateLimits_Increase_OnNodeLeave`) subsequently iterate over **all** services in `SERVICE_NODE_LOCAL_RATE_LIMIT_CONFIGS.keySet()` and assert on their assignments. If the rate-limit calculator populates assignments for different services at different times (or in separate update cycles), waiting on a single service/task-type pair does not guarantee the others are ready, and the tests can still be flaky.\nConsider either:\n- Expanding the helper to iterate over all known services/task types (or at least the ones the calling test will assert on), or\n- Passing the service/task-type to wait for as a parameter, and calling it once per service in the tests that need it.\nThis would make the wait condition match the actual assertions and reduce the risk of intermittent test failures.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/inference/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/inference/common/InferenceServiceNodeLocalRateLimitCalculatorTests.java-x-pack/plugin/inference/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/inference/common/InferenceServiceNodeLocalRateLimitCalculatorTests.java--6869:6912,7515:7558","promptId":"#CJHR1","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/inference/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/inference/common/InferenceServiceNodeLocalRateLimitCalculatorTests.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/inference/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/inference/common/InferenceServiceNodeLocalRateLimitCalculatorTests.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":6869,"endPos":